1
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,500
[waves crashing]

2
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,160
ELIAS: Nobody comes out to Gull
Rock unless they're lost or running.

3
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,180
MARA: I'm neither. I'm a journalist.
Mara Quinn, from the Harbor Gazette.

4
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:55,440
ELIAS: Then you're lost. Turn the
boat around before the tide does it for you.

5
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:02,280
MARA: Forty years ago the Aurelia
went down two miles from this light.

6
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:08,000
MARA: Eleven sailors. The inquiry
said the lamp was dark that night.

7
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,980
ELIAS: The inquiry said a lot of things.

8
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:18,940
MARA: Your father was the keeper.
I think you know what really happened.

9
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,440
<i>[thunder rumbling]</i>

10
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:34,680
ELIAS: Storm's coming in fast.
You'll have to stay the night.

11
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,240
MARA: Then we have time to talk.

12
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:44,780
ELIAS: Coffee's in the tin. Don't
touch the logbooks on the shelf.

13
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,240
MARA: Why not? Are they the logbooks
from 1979?

14
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:55,180
ELIAS: They're my father's. That's
all you need to know.

15
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:06,680
[glass shatters]

16
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:11,380
MARA: Elias! The window, the wind
broke the window!

17
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:16,800
ELIAS: Get the lamp room shutters,
now! The light can't go dark.

18
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,860
MARA: Is that what happened in
1979? The light went dark?

19
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:28,880
ELIAS: No. The light never went
dark. My father kept it burning all night.

20
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:35,960
ELIAS: He saw the Aurelia. He signaled
her. The captain ignored the signal.

21
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,060
MARA: Then why did the inquiry blame him?

22
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:46,420
ELIAS: Because the shipping company
paid for a different story.

23
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:53,620
ELIAS: The proof is in the logbook.
Page forty-two. Every signal, every hour.

24
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:05,120
[birds calling]

25
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:10,540
MARA: The storm's gone. It's beautiful
out here in the morning.

26
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:17,380
ELIAS: Take the logbook. Print
the truth. My father deserves that much.

27
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,880
MARA: Why trust me with it now?

28
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:27,600
ELIAS: Because last night you ran
toward the light, not away from it.

29
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,960
MARA: I'll make sure everyone knows
the light never went dark.

30
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:42,660
ELIAS: A lighthouse doesn't save
ships, Mara. It only tells them the truth. They still have to listen.

31
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:47,660
